+### R2. Loop-closure bugs in the money audits (B023)
+
+`uvx ruff check --select B023 src/` names **six** modules, not the three in
+the brief: `analysis/bilt_trios.py` (3), `analysis/returned_payments.py` (2),
+`analysis/categorization_audit.py` (3), and additionally
+`analysis/rolling_candidates.py` (2), `analysis/rolling_timing.py` (2) and
+`spine/archive_import.py` (1). All fourteen are the same defect class, all are
+money-weighted, so all were fixed, one commit per module. The extra three are
+flagged in the brief as outside the named list; leaving them would have left
+`B023 src/` non-empty, which is the packet's own definition of done.
+
+At every site the lambda/closure runs during the same loop iteration
+(`apply`, or the heuristic called immediately below its definition), so the
+late binding is **latent, not live** — a refactor that stored the closure and
+called it after the loop advanced would make it live. Each fix binds the loop
+variable as a default argument, and each module got a test with two
+iterations whose values differ, asserting the second does not see the first's
+binding. Those tests pass before and after the fix; that is the "document
+that the call is immediate and the fix is defensive" clause, made executable.
+
+No amount, fee constant or matching rule changed. `B023 src/` is now clean.
+
+### R4. `/api/alerts`
+
+New router `api/routers/alerts.py`, registered in `api/app.py`. Returns
+`[{kind, severity, title, detail, href}]` built from the nine alert-shaped
+`compute_*` functions the brief names. It does not call `build_brief_data`.
+Inputs are read the way the brief reads them (three complete months of audit
+transactions, accounts enriched with card metadata, the raw metadata dict, the
+recovery and archive stores). Silent when clean. `build_due_rows` is passed
+empty FX rates on purpose so the route never reaches the network, and the
+recovery monitor's `uninitialized` state is treated as "no monitor on this
+box", not a money alert — otherwise an isolated spine could never answer `[]`.
+
+Tests (`tests/api/test_alerts.py`): a clean synthetic spine answers `[]`; a
+seeded returned-payment trio answers exactly one `returned_payment` alert; a
+seeded Rolling deviation answers exactly one `rolling_deviation` alert.
+
+### R5. Merchant page
+
+Route `/merchants/:name` and `pages/Merchants.tsx`. Header from
+`/api/transactions/detail?txn_id=_&merchant=…`, a monthly bar grouped
+client-side from `/api/cashflow/scope?merchant=…&debits_only=true`, and the
+rows in `TxnScopeDrawer`'s shape with one-tap recategorise. Window
+(`window`/`from`/`to`) lives in the querystring via `urlState.ts`. The
+palette's merchant results and the merchant name in the detail drawer link
+here; categories and accounts still open a filtered list.
+
+### R6. Notification bell
+
+`useAlerts()` (`['alerts']`, 5-minute stale) and
+`components/NotificationsBell.tsx`, used in both the desktop and mobile
+headers. Count only when non-zero; tapping lists each alert's severity, title,
+detail and href; Escape or a click outside closes it.
+
+**Deviation:** the brief names a Radix popover. `@radix-ui/react-popover` is
+not in `package.json` or `package-lock.json`, and the allowed command set
+cannot run `npm install`, so the anchored panel and its Escape handling are
+local. This is a decision to revisit only if the operator wants the
+dependency added.
+
+### F3 (tier 3). Budget PATCH + pace tick
+
+`AccountMetadataStore.set_budget_category` and `PATCH /api/budget`. A PATCH,
+not a PUT: only the category in the body is written, through the metadata
+store's existing lock-and-reload, so no other budget line, account entry or
+top-level key is touched. `BudgetBar` draws a pace tick at the projected
+end-of-month spend as a share of the limit.
+
+Design choice kept small: the endpoint's response is the single written
+entry; the UI edit surface is the pace tick only (no inline Planned editor).
+
+### G1 (tier 3). CSV importer
+
+`components/CsvImportDialog.tsx`, opened from the Transactions toolbar.
+Reads a CSV with a transaction id column and a category and/or note column,
+previews the row count and the exact edit, and only then calls
+`POST /api/transactions/edit-operations` followed by `…/apply`. The
+Transactions export now carries `id`, so the round trip works. `fromCsv` (RFC
+4180, BOM-stripping) was added to `lib/csv.ts` as the inverse of the exporter.
+
+Design choice kept small: one operation, one edit — every row must carry the
+same category and the same note. A mixed file is refused rather than split
+into several operations.
+
+### C3 (tier 3). Saved views
+
+`GET/PUT /api/views`, stored under the top-level `saved_views` key through
+the metadata store's lock. The palette lists saved views and can save the
+current location as one (prompt for a name). A `path` must start with `/` so a
+view cannot be a protocol-relative URL. Deleting a view was not requested and
+was not added.
